## <custom data-type="emoji" data-id="id-0">:person_with_crown:</custom> User Story

**As a** shopper looking to browse products by brand, **I want** to view all available brands grouped alphabetically, **so that** I can quickly find a specific brand and explore its product offerings.

| Alphabetical Grouping Brands are listed A–Z, grouped under corresponding letter headings. Non-alphabetic characters (e.g., numbers, symbols) are grouped and positioned before A–Z | [mobile brand list](https://www.figma.com/design/fU79c88OUWKPwScoPQ0Yag/laioutr-CMS?node-id=276-97391&t=2FpqZago9DvoDz6H-4) [desktop brand list](https://www.figma.com/design/fU79c88OUWKPwScoPQ0Yag/laioutr-CMS?node-id=276-113560&t=2FpqZago9DvoDz6H-4) ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=706fd84f-caba-4290-b1fa-f07ff6236000&&collection=&height=544&occurrenceKey=null&width=420&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null) |
| --- | --- |
| Link Behavior Each brand name is a link to its individual brand detail/product page. Links open in the same tab unless configured otherwise. [Use internal brand list link with amount pill](https://www.figma.com/design/92moLelAY8lh8mI0rhCGzy/laioutr-UI?node-id=20214-5383&t=trMEQiF1AD9o3Leb-4) | ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=d62b4089-0324-41c9-b255-abd3e9c67d07&&collection=&height=480&occurrenceKey=null&width=360&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null)  |
| **Layout** has optional "Top brands" section under the title (Logo Slider) has content slot after brand list  | ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=f91f74dc-db6b-4512-9ad9-b14ad27ad783&&collection=&height=317&occurrenceKey=null&width=246&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null) if the top brands section is hidden, hide the separator under it too (so that no two separators can be seen directly one after the other)  |
| **SEO** URL Structure URL: `/brands/` (canonical) Brand page links should follow a clean, SEO-friendly format HTML Markup Use semantic HTML (`<section>`, `<h2>`, `<ul>`, `<li>`, `<a>`) for brand groupings. Use meaningful heading structure: `h1` for the page title, `h2` for alphabet letters, `h3` optional under each section. Internal Linking All brand links should be crawlable by search engines (no JavaScript-only rendering). Ensure each brand has a dedicated page linked from this overview. Meta Tags Custom `<title>` and `<meta description>` for `/brands/` page. Structured data (e.g., `ItemList` schema) can be added to improve search engine understanding. |  |
| **Accessibility**  Semantic HTML Use correct ARIA roles (e.g., `role="navigation"` for the letter index). Use `<nav aria-label="Brand alphabet navigation">` for the A–Z index. Keyboard Navigation All links must be accessible via keyboard (tab and enter). Skip link provided to bypass navigation and jump to main content. Screen Reader Support Letter groupings should be announced properly (e.g., "Section A – Brands starting with A").  |  |
| **Non-Functional Requirements** **Performance**: Fast loading using pagination or lazy loading if there are hundreds of brands. **Scalability**: Can support hundreds of brands without degrading performance. **Accessibility**: Meet WCAG 2.1 AA compliance. **SEO**: Structured, crawlable HTML and keyword-optimized copy. |  |

### **Acceptance Criteria:**

* create example like figma , add top brands section , product slider and CMS text image slots

